!/coresight_mode
# Bare patterns like `*.o` only match at the build-context ROOT with this
# Docker/BuildKit version, not recursively into subdirectories -- confirmed
# via an isolated test (a file at src/foo.o was NOT excluded by a bare
# `*.o` line, but was excluded once written as `**/*.o`). Found the hard
# way: stray root-owned .o files left in src/ from an unrelated earlier
# host-side build (a different, incompatible GCC/LTO version) were still
# getting copied into aflplusplus-reusing_fuzzer_only's build context and
# silently shadowing the container's own freshly-built objects, breaking
# the link with an LTO bytecode version mismatch.
**/*.dSYM
**/*.o
**/*.pyc
**/*.so
.sync_tmp
.test
.test2
.git
.dockerignore
.github
CITATION.cff
CONTRIBUTING.md
Changelog.md
Dockerfile
LICENSE
